From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AX23_V2_OPENWRT <ax23-v2-openwrt@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:56:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: ath11k: low-memory RX rings follow the reference
 profiles

Adversarial review of 960: the IPQ5018 RXDMA buffer ring (512) and the
RXDMA error destination ring (128) matched none of the published
low-memory profiles. Use 1024 for the buffer ring on both radios and keep
the error ring at its default. See the patch description.
---
 ...-rings-follow-the-reference-profiles.patch | 65 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 65 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/962-wifi-ath11k-low-memory-RX-rings-follow-the-reference-profiles.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/962-wifi-ath11k-low-memory-RX-rings-follow-the-reference-profiles.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/962-wifi-ath11k-low-memory-RX-rings-follow-the-reference-profiles.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..acb55bd797
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/962-wifi-ath11k-low-memory-RX-rings-follow-the-reference-profiles.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+From: AX23_V2_OPENWRT project
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: low-memory RX rings follow the reference profiles
+
+Review of 960 against the three published low-memory profiles (the
+ath-next "use smaller DP rings on low-memory systems" proposal, OpenWrt
+PR #21495 and the QSDK 512M profile) found two values none of them uses:
+
+- RXDMA buffer ring 512 on IPQ5018. Every reference uses 1024 (QSDK
+  4096); 512 was only ever measured, on a QCN6122, to overflow under
+  upload bursts. Use 1024 on both radios. Cost: ~1.4 MiB on IPQ5018.
+- RXDMA error destination ring 128. No reference reduces it (all keep
+  1024). It is a hardware-produced descriptor ring with no pre-posted
+  buffers, so 128 saved only ~28 KiB per radio while risking RXDMA
+  back-pressure if an error burst outruns the host. Keep the default.
+
+Monitor/status ring sizes are unchanged (QSDK 512M / ath-next values).
+---
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+index 71808b1..04024b9 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+@@ -233,13 +233,15 @@ struct ath11k_pdev_dp {
+ /* Host RX ring sizes used when the radio runs in FW memory mode 2
+  * ("qcom,ath11k-fw-memory-mode = <2>", 256 MiB boards). The default sizes
+  * above pre-post ~9200 2 KiB RX buffers per radio, which a 256 MiB IPQ5018
+- * board with two radios cannot afford. Values follow the QSDK 512M profile
+- * for the monitor/status rings; the RXDMA buffer ring is 512 for IPQ5018
+- * and 1024 for QCN6122, which overflows at 512 under upload bursts.
++ * board with two radios cannot afford. The RXDMA buffer ring is 1024 for
++ * both radios, the value of the ath-next low-memory profile and of OpenWrt
++ * PR #21495 (512 was measured to overflow on a QCN6122 under upload bursts).
++ * The monitor/status rings follow the QSDK 512M profile. The RXDMA error
++ * destination ring keeps its default: it holds no pre-posted buffers, so
++ * shrinking it saves only ~28 KiB per radio while risking RXDMA back-pressure
++ * during an error burst; no reference profile reduces it.
+  */
+-#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM		512
+-#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM_QCN6122	1024
+-#define DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM	128
++#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM		1024
+ #define DP_RXDMA_MON_STATUS_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM	512
+ #define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_BUF_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM	128
+ #define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DST_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM	128
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+index bf07649..65d4535 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+@@ -586,14 +586,10 @@ static int ath11k_dp_rx_ring_size(struct ath11k_base *ab,
+ 
+ 	switch (ring) {
+ 	case ATH11K_DP_RX_RING_BUF:
+-		if (!lowmem)
+-			return DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE;
+-		return ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_QCN6122_HW10 ?
+-		       DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM_QCN6122 :
+-		       DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM;
++		return lowmem ? DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM :
++				DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE;
+ 	case ATH11K_DP_RX_RING_ERR_DST:
+-		return lowmem ? DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM :
+-				DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE;
++		return DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE;
+ 	case ATH11K_DP_RX_RING_MON_STATUS:
+ 		return lowmem ? DP_RXDMA_MON_STATUS_RING_SIZE_LOWMEM :
+ 				DP_RXDMA_MON_STATUS_RING_SIZE;
